x87 inline fast path: generate the 53-bit common case as TCG ops.

Patch 05 does the common x87 case on the host FPU inside the helpers; the
remaining cost is the helper call structure itself (every op is a call,
the value round-trips env->ft0/fpregs, fp_status flags are saved and
merged). This patch adds five scalar binary64 opcodes to TCG
(add/sub/mul/div/fmsub_f64 on raw bit patterns in i64 temps, lowered to
VEX scalar SSE with FMA3 on x86-64 and to fadd/fsub/fmul/fdiv/fnmsub on
aarch64) and an inline translator path (target/i386/tcg/x87-inline.c.inc)
for fld/fst/fstp m64, the six arithmetic ops with m64 and st(i) operands
(incl. the popping forms), fld st(i), fxch, fst/fstp st(i). The same
checks as x87f_binop() run inline, branchless, before any state is
touched; anything that fails branches to the unchanged helper sequence,
so results and the status word stay identical to softfloat. Only PC=53,
RC=nearest, PE masked is inlined (env->x87_fast_mode, derived from fpuc
by update_fp_status(); the x87-fast=off property turns it off).

Measured on a Ryzen 7 5700X with the DOS loop of tools/x87-guest-test.py
(ns per x87 op): softfloat 22.8, patch 05 helpers 10.6, this patch 6.9.
tools/x87-guest-test.py (extended to every inlined form plus a PE-unmasked
control word): 298,460 result lines identical with the fast path on/off.
The aarch64 lowering is written against llvm-mc encodings but has not run
yet (needs the M1 Air).
